# Order replacement walkthrough: one scenario per documented rule.
# Two asks at 100 (1 is ahead of 2) and one at 103.
L S 1 100 10
L S 2 100 10
L S 3 103 5
# Rule 1: same price, smaller quantity -> reduced in place, keeps time priority.
R 1 100 4
# Rule 2: same price, larger quantity -> loses priority (now behind 2).
R 1 100 6
# Proof: a buy for 12 @ 100 now fills 2 (10) before 1 (2).
L B 10 100 12
# Rule 3: a price change loses priority and may cross: move bid 11 up to 103.
L B 11 99 8
R 11 103 8
# Rule 4: unknown, filled and cancelled ids are rejected.
R 99 100 1
R 10 100 1
C 3
R 3 103 1
# Rule 5: invalid quantity / price are rejected with the usual reasons and leave
# the order untouched (bid 20 keeps 7 @ 95). bad_tick is covered by unit tests,
# since this fixture uses tick 1.
L B 20 95 7
R 20 95 0
R 20 95 4294967297
R 20 0 7
R 20 100001 7
# Rule 6: same price, same quantity -> no-op that keeps priority.
R 20 95 7
